tion  um in the anti-pdl one treated mice  the uh the uh peptide specific cells  retain the ability to produce interferon  gamma in an ex vivo restimulation  experiment  uh more effectively than in untreated  mice  um this is quantified on the right so  we're comparing untreated mice to pdl  one blockade treated mice this is at the  three weeks after tumor cell injection  time point and look look in particular  here at the cells isolated from these  tumors we have a higher proportion  of cda t cells able to produce  interferon gamma in response to click  beetle peptide restimulation in a cell  culture dish for four hours  so that would suggest that treatment  helps t cells either  either one retain function  or b  potentially a new wave of effector t  cells is stimulated from the spleens of  these mice  okay so  the next observation was i mentioned  earlier that our that leg 3 may be a  better  marker of t cell exhaustion than pd1  our best marker of t cell activation  turns out in this system is klrg1  expression  and it appears to be  more or less a binary choice for an  individual t cell to become either  a leg three positive exhausted cell or a  klr g1 positive effector cell  following treatment  and at about at about the time  that i was going to start  um combining therapies a paper came out  in a different model of cancer it was a  melanoma paper  where they combined pd-1 blockade with  pdl-1 blockade with a hypothesis that  pd-1 blockade would activate t-cells and  pdl-1 blockade would activate the  macrophages  and in that paper  they saw a benefit of this dual therapy  and i  thought that would be cool to try in  this system so we did and i was agnostic  on whether  pdl one blockade was activating  macrophages or not but we gave the dual  therapy a shot  and in the green line here you can see  that we cured half of those mice that  was really  satisfying  we did a lot of treatments here we  treated these mice with both pd-1 and  pdl-1 blockade from day 7 t