ying  to interrogate what that was that was  driving all of these exhaustion markers  is to look in some of the clinical  databases  for  either cytokines or chemokines or growth  factors  that either the tumor cells themselves  express or the myeloid cells in the  tumors expressed that correlate with  impaired patient survival so we're  trying to find something that's  clinically relevant here  and it's really hard to make pancreas  cancer survival worse i spent a lot of  time in the database trying to find  something  il-27 is one of those things so high  expression of il-27 p28 within pancreas  cancer  actually makes pancreas cancer survival  worse  so lucky for us there's a reporter mouse  for il-27  cells that are expressing il-27 gene  those cells also express gfp  and as a proportion of cd45 positive  immune cells the proportion making il-27  goes up over time in the tumors  suggesting that our mouse model may be  reflecting what's happening in the human  disease where il-27 is not  useful  and this is weird and interesting  because il-27 is critical for t-cell  priming  and is actually really important in the  response elicited by type 1 dendritic  cells after vaccination  which is a topic for another time  but is why i was aware of this field  il-27 is really important for t-cell  priming and memory formation but too  much may be a bad thing  we did another time course and we  characterized which  myeloid cells in this case or non t  cells that are in the tumor are  expressing il 27 at either day 7 14 or  21 after tumor cell injection and at day  7 it was clearly granulocytes or  neutrophils that are  the main source of il27  at day 14 it was a mix of type 2  dendritic cells which in this case in  our gaining scheme are serb alpha  positive  along with macrophages tumor-associated  myelin macrophages  and some other cells including type 1  dendritic cells at day 14  and then several cell types of day 21 so  essentially our t cells that go into our  tumors  